  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P0] Return `id`, not `userId`, to satisfy the declared `User` contract",
      "body": "`loadUser` declares `Promise<User>`, and `User` is still `{ id: string; name: string }` (src/users.ts:7), but the changed return line produces `{ userId: row.id, name: row.display_name }`. This fails type-checking under standard TypeScript (missing required property `id`, excess property `userId`, error TS2322), and even in transpile-only setups every successful lookup returns an object whose `.id` is `undefined` for consumers of the typed contract. The break is deterministic — it occurs on every input that finds a row — so it is blocking despite no other callers currently existing in the repo.",
      "severity": "P0",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/users.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 12,
        "end": 12
      }
    }
  ],
